ther of Osman I and a legendary figure in Turkish history, the mosque reflects the cultural and spiritual aspirations of the Turkmen people as they navigate their identity in a modern world. Its significance is underscored by its role in unifying various Islamic practices in a region historically influenced by diverse religious traditions, thereby acting as a beacon of faith and cultural identity for the Turkmen nation.

